course: dictionary
lesson: 10065
title: Textbook in school and in sport
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A textbook is a book that pupils and students use to study a subject. Maths, science and history all have their own textbooks, and you use them with lessons and exercises. «Open your textbooks at page twelve» tells you the book is something you hold and read.
explain: Textbook can also be an adjective, a describing word. «A textbook goal» means a goal done exactly as it should be, a perfect example of the rules. Read the words around the word to see which meaning fits: a book in your bag, or something done perfectly.
explain: Packing the bag for school, you will hear the things inside: "pidrUchnyk" (textbook), "zOshyt" (exercise book), "ruchka" (pen), "olIvets" (pencil), and the bag itself, "ryukzAk". Pidruchnyk is the Ukrainian word for textbook, so the same thing has different names in different languages.
fact: A textbook is a book used by pupils and students to study a subject.
fact: «Maths textbook» and «science textbook» name the subject the book is about.
fact: As an adjective, «textbook» means exactly as it should be, a perfect example.
fact: «A textbook example» is one that shows a rule or idea very clearly.
fact: In Ukrainian, «pidrUchnyk» means textbook, and «zOshyt» means exercise book.
exercise: «Open your textbooks at page twelve.» What is a textbook? | A ball used in a game | A bag for carrying lunch | *A book used by pupils to study a subject | A pen for writing notes
exercise: «The gymnast made a textbook landing.» What does textbook mean here? | Made of paper and card | Done in the dark | Very slow and very late | *Done perfectly, exactly by the rules
exercise: In Ukrainian, «pidrUchnyk» means which of these? | School bag | Pencil | Pen | *Textbook
test: Packing the bag, a pupil picks up a «maths textbook». What subject is the book about? | *Maths | Music | Sport | Art
test: «That was a textbook case of a bad mistake.» What does textbook suggest? | A broken box | A court case | A case for holding books | *A perfect example of its kind
exam: Which sentence uses textbook as an adjective? | «Put your textbook in your bag.» | *«It was a textbook goal, perfect in every way.» | «Our science textbook has lots of pictures.» | «Open your textbooks at page ten.»
